{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And he said, HaShem.</b> With alef dalet." "<b>[Grace in your eyes</b> like before you]. Do not, please, pass from over your servant — Rashi's interpretation: to the greatest of them all he said, etc. And how did he recognize the greatest? He saw them walking on the road like a teacher and his two students — the teacher in the middle, the greater one to his right and the smaller one to his left. This is what we learned, and so we find with the three angels who came to Abraham — Michael in the middle, Gabriel to his right, and Raphael to his left. And further Rashi interpreted: even though it is written afterward 'and he ran toward them,' the speech was beforehand. And if you ask: but we say in Pesaḥim — for a single matter, what is earlier is earlier and what is later is later. Rather, what Rashi interpreted here — we do not assess it by the rule of earlier and later, but by the rule of inverted verse order."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {1 "The bracketed heading appears already bracketed in the source; Rashi's interpretation is paraphrased with 'etc.' where Chizkuni writes וכו׳."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:36.290151451Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}